+# Circuit Debugger — Contract
+
+## `simulate(gates, inputs)`
+
+- [x] Returns values for all input wires unchanged -> simulate with inputs only, no gates returns inputs
+- [x] AND gate computes logical AND -> {a:1,b:1}->1, {a:1,b:0}->0, {a:0,b:0}->0
+- [x] OR gate computes logical OR -> {a:1,b:0}->1, {a:0,b:0}->0, {a:1,b:1}->1
+- [x] XOR gate computes logical XOR -> {a:1,b:0}->1, {a:1,b:1}->0, {a:0,b:0}->0
+- [x] Chained gates evaluate in dependency order -> gate B depends on gate A's output, both resolve correctly
+- [x] Gates given out of dependency order still resolve -> shuffle gate array, same result
+- [x] Returns every wire (inputs + all gate outputs) -> result has key for each
+- [x] A correct n-bit adder computes X+Y=Z -> build adder, feed bits, decode z == x+y
+- [x] Deep dependency chains resolve -> 45-bit adder simulates correctly
+
+## `findSwappedWires(gates)`
+
+- [x] Correct adder (no swaps) returns [] -> generated clean adder -> []
+- [x] Detects a single swapped pair (returns both wires sorted) -> swap z/internal, find both
+- [x] Detects 4 swapped pairs (8 wires) -> generate adder, apply 4 swaps, returns exactly those 8 sorted
+- [x] Result is sorted ascending -> output equals output.slice().sort()
+- [x] Works on many random 8..45-bit adders with 4 random (detectable) swaps -> returns exact swapped set
+- [x] Completes a 45-bit (~220 gate) circuit in well under 5 seconds -> timed test
+
+## Quality
+
+- [x] `npm run build` clean
+- [x] `npm run lint` clean
+- [x] `npm test` all pass
